==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|witchhunt|witch hunt}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|witch|hunt}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈwɪtʃhʌnt/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[witch]]-[[hunt]]}}

# {{lb|en|now|chiefly|historical}} A search for people believed to be using [[sorcery]] or [[harmful]] [[magic]], typically in order to [[persecute]] or [[punish]] them.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1885|author=w:H. Rider Haggard|title=King Solomon's Mines
|passage=To-night ye will see. It is the great '''witch-hunt''', and many will be smelt out as wizards and slain.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=w:Ronald Hutton|title=The Witch|page=27|publisher=Yale University Press|year_published=2018
|passage=The rupturing of British rule over India in the rebellion of 1857 permitted a great '''witch-hunt''', with lethal effects, to occur among the tribes of northern India.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} An [[attempt]] to find and [[punish]] or [[harass]] a group of people perceived as a [[threat]], usually on [[ideological]] or [[political]] [[ground]]s.
#* {{RQ:Orwell Homage|passage=Rank-and-file Communists everywhere are led away on a senseless '''witch-hunt''' after '[[Trotskyist]]s'.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[public]] or [[political]] [[campaign]] or investigation which [[smear]]s a person or group.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Mike Adams|title=Feminists Say the Darndest Things: A Politically Incorrect Professor Confronts "Womyn" on Campus|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9781101217832
|passage=Even fewer people could believe that the UNCW administration would actually undertake a '''witch hunt''' against me, even going so far as to invoke their right to read my personal e-mails because they were on the university&#39;s system.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Hugh Maguire|title=My First 40 Jobs: A Memoir|publisher=iUniverse|isbn=9781475901375|page=308
|passage=I defended myself vigorously on that complaint as well; also mentioning that Julie Ann Wilks had always disliked me and had been conducting “a '''witch hunt'''”  against me. As soon as I said the words “'''witch hunt'''” Katy interrupted and wouldn't let me continue {{...}}}}
#* '''2016''' May 15, Donald Trump, tweet quoted in '''2019''', Lindy West, ''The Witches Are Coming'', Hachette Books ({{ISBN|9780316449892}})
#*:  The media is really on a '''witch-hunt''' against me. False reporting, and plenty of it - but we will prevail!

